A landing no logged hit stands for, at the fight's last logged frame or at the first frame of an away stretch, isn't
counted in the totals, kill or no kill (enginecheck.ts fightTotals). HELD BACK: the check's file, another agent's in
the damage-factors round (2026-11-26); mixed, for the lead to judge.

Why: of the 16 slash2s of Rossi's ultimate in the development logs (scripts/probes/rossi/slash2.py), the 3 without a
Seething Blood extra in the log (207f 42.85 s, 4a64 29.15 and 71.46 s) are each the last logged hit of the fight or
of Si's first life (4a64's away stretch 29.15–51.31 s); no hit by anyone follows within 3 s. The other 13 have their
extra at the slash's ms and bleed ticks after it. So the enemy dies or leaves at that hit and the crit's trigger finds
no target: not Rossi's bleed clock. (The probe's 0c14 199.50 s row is a stab, not a slash2: there the killing hit is
Si's capped combo hit at 199.505 s, and the stab's extra at that ms is logged; so a same-frame trigger can land before
a killing hit that is another one's, and this rule, taking every landing of that frame, is too broad.) The kill rule (a landing after the killing frame) only applies where the log's
total is the enemy's HP or its last hit is capped, which neither log shows.

